; status: works — diagonal fold then a half fold. The half fold scores both
; layers, so --v marks two different lines in the paper; `at #(.a)` picks the
; bottom layer's scar to cross with the bottom edge (crossings are material —
; paper space, never table space)
paper square

@map .c onto .a moving .c
--b = through .a .b
--v = @map .b onto .a
.mid = --b * --v & #[.a]
map .d onto .mid
